n","c":"high","cited":"Hos. v. 1"},{"id":"f0110934e25b","v":"npnf.gregor_gr.regula_pastoralis","w":"gregor_gr.regula_pastoralis","a":"gregor_der_grosse","s":8,"p":[1,1],"r":[4,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Hos. iv. 9"},{"id":"84d80c15335c","v":"npnf.gregor_gr.regula_pastoralis","w":"gregor_gr.regula_pastoralis","a":"gregor_der_grosse","s":37,"p":[0,0],"r":[2,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"Hos. ii. 8","note":"Stellenangabe der Ausgabe (englische Zählung, umgerechnet)"},{"id":"e201704e8b06","v":"npnf.kyrill_jer.catecheses","w":"kyrill_jer.catecheses","a":"cyrillus_von_jerusalem","s":13,"p":[9,9],"r":[4,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Hosea iv. 2."},{"id":"adad0fdaa5ab","v":"npnf.kyrill_jer.catecheses","w":"kyrill_jer.catecheses","a":"cyrillus_von_jerusalem","s":13,"p":[30,30],"r":[2,22],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"Hos. ii. 20.","note":"Stellenangabe der Ausgabe (englische Zählung, umgerechnet)"},{"id":"803f7db7bc76","v":"npnf.kyrill_jer.catecheses","w":"kyrill_jer.catecheses","a":"cyrillus_von_jerusalem","s":15,"p":[21,21],"r":[6,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Hos. vi. 2."},{"id":"9472aa9ee8a8","v":"npnf.kyrill_jer.catecheses","w":"kyrill_jer.catecheses","a":"cyrillus_von_jerusalem","s":15,"p":[24,24],"r":[13,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Hosea xiii. 14."},{"id":"dbe1934ab3e1","v":"npnf.kyrill_jer.catecheses","w":"kyrill_jer.catecheses","a":"cyrillus_von_jerusalem","s":16,"p":[5,5],"r":[4,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Hos. iv. 2."},{"id":"4f8c3a966bd2","v":"npnf.kyrill_jer.catecheses","w":"kyrill_jer.catecheses","a":"cyrillus_von_jerusalem","s":17,"p":[17,17],"r":[4,12],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Hosea iv. 12."},{"id":"d22ac9fbcfc1","v":"lf.kyrill_alex.quod_unus_sit_christus","w":"kyrill_alex.quod_unus_sit_christus","a":"cyrillus_von_alexandrien","s":1,"p":[37,37],"r":[4,8],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"e Elsewhere S. Cyril says, \"For Christ was made for us sin, as it is written. And surely not guilty of sin (for we are not wont so to wander in mind) seeing that He had no knowledge of transgression, being God by Nature and beaming forth of God the Father. But because He has been made a sacrifice for sin (for Christ our Passover was sacrificed for us), therefore do we say that He was made sin also.\" Glaph. 349 c. And in commenting upon Hosea iv. 8, They eat the sin of My people, S. Cyril says, \"A kid therefore of the goats was wont to be sacrificed for sin, wherefore the sacrifice itself was also called sin .\" in xii Proph. 71 b. But the two explanations of being made sin may be but two aspects of what the Holy Ghost tells us in tnese words. S. Athanasius says, \"For as by receiving our infirmities, He is said to be infirm Himself, though not Himself infirm, for He is the Power of God: and He became sin for us and a curse, though not having sinned Himself but because He Himself bare our sins and our curse, so &c.\" Agst Arians. ii. 55 fin. p. 359 O.T. Similarly S. Cyril, \" As therefore He is said to have been infirm though not infirm (for He is the Power of God), because He bare our infirmities, and the Divine Scripture says that He has been made a curse, not meaning that He has been actually transmade into a curse, but that He bare the curse for us, and again He is said to have been made sin, not as forgetful of His own Nature nor passing into sin Who knew it not, but because He took on Him our sins, as it is written, in His body on the Tree, so\" &c. Thes. cap. 15 p. 162 e, see also cap. 32 p. 276 e."},{"id":"7e2f8bbb1a3c","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.orationes","w":"gregor_naz.orationes","a":"gregor_von_nazianz","s":2,"p":[5,5],"r":[3,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Hos. iii. 4."},{"id":"b4879f9a7113","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.oration